--TEST--
`delete` answers a `bool` saying whether this call is what removed the row, so a job a worker holds is reported rather than thrown about — `rule:concurrency/queue-deletion-is-explicit-and-bounded`, `rule:concurrency/cancel-is-a-race-it-can-lose`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A removal is a race the same way a cancellation is: a worker may claim a
// pending job at any moment, and a claimed job is not removable at all. That
// makes "there was nothing left to remove" the ordinary outcome, so it is an
// answer and not an exception — a `void` spelling would make "removed" and
// "too late" look identical at the call site.
var $receipt = Core\Queue::push("jobs/send-receipt.nvs");
bool $gone = Core\Queue::delete($receipt);

// And the answer is that `bool` and nothing wider: there is no count here, and
// no state left over for `status` to be asked about, because the row is gone
// rather than changed.
string $why = Core\Queue::delete($receipt);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `bool`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
